.SH "NAME"
pcre2_get_bsr \- get the \(rsR convention
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBint\fP pcre2_get_bsr(\fBpcre2_compile_context\fP *\fIccontext\fP, \fBuint32_t\fP *\fIlength\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function gets the convention for processing \f(CR\(rsR\fP within a compile context.
The result is zero for success or \fBPCRE2_ERROR_NULL\fP if either argument is \f(CRNULL\fP.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.